From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hubert Chao <hchao@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:25:35 -0700
Subject: [LNA] fix Local Network Access bypass for <link rel="prerender">

<link rel="prerender"> was bypassing LNA checks. Fix this by blocking
all LNA requests from <link rel="prerender"> as there is no UI to hang a
permission prompt on.

Add

bool IsNoStatePrefetch(content::WebContents* web_contents);

to ContentBrowserClient to allow for content layer to figure out if a
web_contents is a no-state-prefetch (and therefore won't be visible to
the user).

It would be possible, though more work, to check if the correct
permission was granted for the initiator and only block if the
permission wasn't granted. Blocking all LNA requests from link
rel="prerender" is safe though, as these are just considered hints.

